vecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/legalcode"><citetitle>Creative Commons Attribution (CC-BY) 4.0 License</citetitle></ulink>.</para></intellectualRights><coverage><geographicCoverage><boundingCoordinates><westBoundingCoordinate>-79.28637</westBoundingCoordinate><eastBoundingCoordinate>-79.24874</eastBoundingCoordinate><northBoundingCoordinate>40.1683</northBoundingCoordinate><southBoundingCoordinate>40.13025</southBoundingCoordinate></boundingCoordinates></geographicCoverage><temporalCoverage><rangeOfDates><beginDate><calendarDate>2013-06-03</calendarDate></beginDate><endDate><calendarDate>2025-07-07</calendarDate></endDate></rangeOfDates></temporalCoverage><taxonomicCoverage><generalTaxonomicCoverage>Aves</generalTaxonomicCoverage><taxonomicClassification><taxonRankName>class</taxonRankName><taxonRankValue>Aves</taxonRankValue><commonName>Birds</commonName></taxonomicClassification></taxonomicCoverage></coverage><contact><individualName><givenName>Kathryn</givenName><surName>Sullivan</surName></individualName><organizationName>Carnegie Museum of Natural History</organizationName><positionName>Data Scientist</positionName><address><city>Pittsburgh</city><country>US</country></address><electronicMailAddress>sullivank@carnegiemnh.org</electronicMailAddress><userId directory="http://orcid.org/">https://orcid.org/0000-0003-3792-2538</userId></contact><methods><sampling><studyExtent><description><para>Powdermill Nature Reserve (PNR) – the Carnegie Museum of Natural History’s (CMNH) environmental research center located near Rector, Pennsylvania</para></description></studyExtent><samplingDescription><para>The sampling design consists of a contiguous grid of 120-meter blocks overlaid across the main area of PNR. Each block has a central point from which point counts are conducted within a 150 meter radius. The entire nature reserve is split into 10 sectors and there are between 8 and 11 points in each sector, with one sector sampled per day, twice during the breeding season.</para></samplingDescription></sampling><qualityControl><description><para>Original data is captured on paper datasheets which are retained after entry into a Microsoft access database. Most of the data entry follows controlled fields to prevent typos.  After surveys, data were checked by the surveyor, followed by PNR staff at two different stages.</para></description></qualityControl></methods><project><title>Powdermill Nature Reserve: Biotic Change Over Time</title><personnel><individualName><givenName>Kathryn</givenName><surName>Sullivan</surName></individualName><userId directory="http://orcid.org/">https://orcid.org/0000-0003-3792-2538</userId><role>Principal Investigator</role></personnel><abstract><para>Toward undertaking an integrated data analysis to develop resources that position Powdermill Nature Reserve as a regional leader in characterizing long-term change.</para></abstract><funding><para>Richard King Mellon Foundation</para></funding></project></dataset><additionalMetadata><metadata><gbif><dateStamp>2026-08-11T19:20:01.758Z</dateStamp><hierarchyLevel>dataset</hierarchyLevel><collection><parentCollectionIdentifier>CMNH</parentCollectionIdentifier><collectionIdentifier>PNR</collectionIdentifier><collectionName>Powdermill Nature Reserve</collectionName></collection></gbif></metadata></additionalMetadata></eml:eml>